WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.260 --> 00:00:01.300
- Hey guys, it's Justine,

00:00:01.300 --> 00:00:03.580
and today is November 17th, 2018

00:00:03.580 --> 00:00:05.220
and it is the grand reopening

00:00:05.220 --> 00:00:07.350
of the brand new 3rd Street Apple Store,

00:00:07.350 --> 00:00:09.990
and this whole street has such
a special place in my heart,

00:00:09.990 --> 00:00:10.970
because this is the first place

00:00:10.970 --> 00:00:13.070
that I ever came when I was in Los Angeles

00:00:13.070 --> 00:00:15.130
and it's what made me fall
in love with this city.

00:00:15.130 --> 00:00:16.710
It's what made me move here.

00:00:16.710 --> 00:00:19.060
And the fact that I'm here
again for the reopening

00:00:19.060 --> 00:00:20.690
of this store is incredible.

00:00:20.690 --> 00:00:22.380
I was here at the original grand opening

00:00:22.380 --> 00:00:23.720
that happened in 2012.

00:00:23.720 --> 00:00:25.320
Before that, the store was located

00:00:25.320 --> 00:00:26.720
a little bit further down, on 3rd Street,

00:00:26.720 --> 00:00:28.070
and that store opened in 2003,

00:00:28.070 --> 00:00:30.390
which was way before the
iPhone even came out,

00:00:30.390 --> 00:00:31.600
which is crazy to think,

00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:34.063
that there was a time before the iPhone.

00:00:35.845 --> 00:00:37.540
(electronic music)
(pedestrians chatting)

00:00:37.540 --> 00:00:39.430
I'm sorry, I got lost in
looking at the Apple logo.

00:00:39.430 --> 00:00:42.347
(electronic music)

00:00:56.126 --> 00:00:56.959
There you are!

00:00:56.959 --> 00:00:58.442
The Apple Store is about to open!

00:00:58.442 --> 00:00:59.859
Come on, let's go, let's go!

00:00:59.859 --> 00:01:02.942
(customers clapping)

00:01:05.820 --> 00:01:07.930
This is so awesome!

00:01:07.930 --> 00:01:11.282
(customers cheering)

00:01:11.282 --> 00:01:14.806
(electronic music)

00:01:14.806 --> 00:01:15.985
Yay!

00:01:15.985 --> 00:01:20.985
(customers clapping)
(electronic music)

00:01:24.793 --> 00:01:26.145
Hello!

00:01:26.145 --> 00:01:27.543
Yay!

00:01:27.543 --> 00:01:28.561
- We've traded.

00:01:28.561 --> 00:01:29.966
- We've traded places!

00:01:29.966 --> 00:01:31.440
- This is crazy, you're clapping me in!

00:01:31.440 --> 00:01:33.669
- He has fixed so many iPhones for me.

00:01:33.669 --> 00:01:36.252
(upbeat music)

00:01:37.831 --> 00:01:41.760
In 2012, when this store first opened,

00:01:41.760 --> 00:01:44.190
I was here dancing in a panda onesie.

00:01:44.190 --> 00:01:45.880
I'm not gonna do that this year,

00:01:45.880 --> 00:01:48.101
but let's never forget
where we started from.

00:01:48.101 --> 00:01:51.268
(upbeat guitar music)

00:01:54.698 --> 00:01:56.520
Let's take a quick little walkthrough.

00:01:56.520 --> 00:01:58.030
One of the things that you'll notice,

00:01:58.030 --> 00:02:00.070
is they now have a living wall

00:02:00.070 --> 00:02:01.030
and they have these trees,

00:02:01.030 --> 00:02:03.320
that are the same trees that
they have at Apple Park Campus.

00:02:03.320 --> 00:02:06.330
They are called, let me read
it to you, just to make sure

00:02:06.330 --> 00:02:08.150
I don't mess the name of these trees up.

00:02:08.150 --> 00:02:11.393
They are triple-trunk ficus trees.

00:02:11.393 --> 00:02:14.976
(relaxed electronic music)

00:02:25.845 --> 00:02:26.678
So what do you think of the store?

00:02:26.678 --> 00:02:28.100
How long have you worked here?

00:02:28.100 --> 00:02:31.280
- This store I've been at
for about, since August 2016,

00:02:31.280 --> 00:02:33.360
at Apple since 2014,

00:02:33.360 --> 00:02:34.980
but this has been,

00:02:34.980 --> 00:02:38.030
I've never seen retail
quite like this, ironically.

00:02:38.030 --> 00:02:40.730
The video monitor, it's
amazing, it's an 8K monitor.

00:02:40.730 --> 00:02:41.563
- [Justine] Yeah.

00:02:41.563 --> 00:02:42.570
- 37 feet wide, I think,

00:02:42.570 --> 00:02:44.850
and then tall, it's like 15 or 17,

00:02:44.850 --> 00:02:46.079
something like that.
- So you're saying

00:02:46.079 --> 00:02:47.320
it's like the biggest video
wall in the United States?

00:02:47.320 --> 00:02:48.620
- In the United States,

00:02:48.620 --> 00:02:51.070
it's the same as the biggest in China,

00:02:51.070 --> 00:02:51.903
I believe.
- Wow.

00:02:51.903 --> 00:02:53.417
- For one of our stores.

00:02:53.417 --> 00:02:54.250
- It's beautiful.

00:02:54.250 --> 00:02:57.167
(electronic music)

00:03:24.367 --> 00:03:25.210
- Hey!

00:03:25.210 --> 00:03:27.893
- How are you, hello.
- Hello!

00:03:27.893 --> 00:03:29.476
- It's Alex and Ed.

00:03:30.566 --> 00:03:31.948
Look, some things are happening.

00:03:31.948 --> 00:03:34.839
- In just a moment, I'm
gonna turn it over to Tim.

00:03:34.839 --> 00:03:37.060
(background noise drowns out speaker)

00:03:37.060 --> 00:03:39.977
(electronic music)

00:03:45.114 --> 00:03:45.947
- This is Matt.

00:03:45.947 --> 00:03:48.350
He was first in line here
at the Apple store today.

00:03:48.350 --> 00:03:50.200
How does it feel to be first in line?

00:03:51.290 --> 00:03:52.707
- It feels crazy.

00:03:53.725 --> 00:03:54.608
I'm a fanboy.

00:03:54.608 --> 00:03:57.469
- Oh my God, this is so great,
it was so nice to meet you.

00:03:57.469 --> 00:03:59.740
Thank you guys so much for
coming with me on this journey.

00:03:59.740 --> 00:04:01.210
This store means so much to me,

00:04:01.210 --> 00:04:02.600
and I'm so glad that you can be here

00:04:02.600 --> 00:04:03.865
and experience it with me.

00:04:03.865 --> 00:04:05.608
I'll see you guys later, bye.

00:04:05.608 --> 00:04:08.525
(electronic music)

